It's easier than that and you don't need to waste a charge.

There are 4 magic cloaks (opera cloak, piece of cloth, tattered cape,
ornamental cope).  They get randomized between invisibility,
displacement, protection, and magic resistance.

Since the other 3 all identify themselves automatically when you put
them on (unless maybe you have invisibility already?), if you find one
of those 4 and it has no obvious effect then you know it's MR without
further testing.

The other magic cloaks all have fixed descriptions (oilskin: slippery
cloak, alchemy smock: apron, elven: faded pall, dwarvish: hooded cloak,
orcish: coarse mantelet) or no alternative descriptions at all (leather
cloak, robe, mummy wrapping).



